WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.100
Dr Ingeborg Nwachukwu convenes the Capability Sprints at Slop University.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.400
I once wrote the assessment rubric for a leadership course.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.610
Six months on, I went looking for who still used it.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.510
A certificate tells you who finished.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.230
I want to know what they kept.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:20.970
So I go looking.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.440
A sign-in sheet at a community shed.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.380
A food-safety tick box.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.270
A club that's paid up, but not present.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:32.070
I've followed five years of Sprint graduates back to their desks.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.770
Some changes hold.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.620
Others quietly slip back.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.540
Her colleagues cite that work again and again.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:43.450
An h-index of twenty-nine, the second-highest at Slop University.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.070
And eleven hundred and thirty-seven citations.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.700
